abstract: >-
  An openly graded registry of material states that exist only while a drive is
  running - light-induced phases and Floquet-engineered bands - together with a
  machine-readable description layer for the controllability of matter. Version
  0.1.2 records 82 driven states across 58 host materials from six domains, each
  with drive parameters, lifetime, mechanism, an explicit evidence level and a
  primary source with DOI. The searched domains are light-driven throughout;
  non-optical drives are admitted by the schema but not yet surveyed. Compilation
  was AI-assisted under human direction and checked against primary literature. No
  entry has undergone peer review; one entry was revised in September 2026 after
  comments from a domain expert, which was correspondence, not review.
keywords:
  - Floquet engineering
  - light-induced superconductivity
  - photoinduced phase transition
  - charge density wave
  - non-equilibrium materials
  - materials database
  - FAIR data
